                "Corporate governance failures in marketing financial accounting—such as unrecorded liabilities, channel stuffing, premature revenue recognition on customer loyalty points, and unverified programmatic ad spend—expose enterprises to devastating regulatory fines, securities class action lawsuits, and executive terminations. The modern Chief Marketing Officer must establish an ironclad fiduciary governance infrastructure aligned with Sarbanes-Oxley (SOX) Section 404 internal accounting controls, Financial Accounting Standards Board (FASB) ASC 606 standards, and executive compensation scorecards directly tied to economic performance.",
